 "intro": {
  "text": "The Two Knights Defence is a reply to the Italian Game (1.e4 e5 2.Nf3 Nc6 3.Bc4): Black brings out the second knight with 3...Nf6, the knight to f6, and attacks the pawn on e4. White's most aggressive answer, 4.Ng5, the knight to g5, attacks f7 with knight and bishop together. You will learn how to block that attack, and why giving up a pawn for quick, active pieces is a fair deal for Black."
 },
